    "## 1.4 Brute-force posterior estimation"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "b9782880",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "- Compute a gridding approximation of the normalized posterior.\n",
    "    - Use logarithm transformations for better numerical stability.\n",
    "- Compute the marginal posterior distributions of $\\alpha$ and $\\beta$ from the gridding approximation.\n",
    "- Using the grid-based approximation of the posterior, compute the posterior mean of $\\alpha$ and $\\beta$."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "74b78d4a",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "c = np.sum(UP_norm)\n",
    "normalized_posterior = UP_norm / c"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "c9fad8a8",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "print(f\"Constant of normalizzazion c: {c:.4e}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Verify sum = 1: {np.sum(normalized_posterior):.10f}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "1c8eeec8",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Now we can perform the discrete marginalization of the joint posterior to obtain the marginal posterior distributions for $\\alpha$ and $\\beta$.\n",
    "\n",
    "$$ P(\\alpha | y) = \\int P(\\alpha, \\beta | y) d\\beta \\approx \\sum_{j} P(\\alpha, \\beta_j | y) \\Delta \\beta $$\n",
    "\n",
    "$$P(\\beta | y) = \\int P(\\alpha, \\beta | y) d\\alpha \\approx \\sum_{i} P(\\alpha_i, \\beta | y) \\Delta \\alpha $$\n",
    "\n",
    "Where $\\Delta \\alpha$ and $\\Delta \\beta$ are the grid step sizes for $\\alpha$ and $\\beta$, respectively."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "33e24bf9",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "marginal_alpha_unnorm = np.sum(UP_norm, axis=0) \n",
    "marginal_beta_unnorm = np.sum(UP_norm, axis=1)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "31886686",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "And finlly we can normalize the marginals:\n",
    "$$ p(\\alpha | y) = \\frac{P(\\alpha | y)}{\\sum_{i} P(\\alpha_i | y) \\Delta \\alpha} $$\n",
    "$$ p(\\beta | y) = \\frac{P(\\beta | y)}{\\sum_{j} P(\\beta_j | y) \\Delta \\beta} $$"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "adc9cea5",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "#to compute density marginals we need the step sizes and sums over axes\n",
    "d_alpha = alpha_vec[1] - alpha_vec[0]\n",
    "d_beta = beta_vec[1] - beta_vec[0]\n",
    "\n",
    "marginal_alpha = marginal_alpha_unnorm / (np.sum(marginal_alpha_unnorm) * d_alpha)\n",
    "marginal_beta = marginal_beta_unnorm / (np.sum(marginal_beta_unnorm) * d_beta)"
   ]
